<title>JAPAN: Advantest soars above 10,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Advantest soars above 10,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Advantest Corp, a maker of semiconductor testing devices, soared above the 10,000 yen barrier for the first time in 13 years, partly helped by high-tech shares' record winning streak in New York, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0130 GMT, the shares had surged by 330 yen to 10,200 yen, a new high for this calendar year. Volume was 592,600 shares.</p>
<p>Shares of another semiconductor-related issue, Tokyo Electron Ltd, hit a 13-year high on Tuesday. The shares stood 520 yen higher at 7,170 at 0131 GMT.</p>
